  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ROOST PROTECTION AND HABITAT CREATION FOR THE WHITE-SHOULDERED IBIS IN NORTHERN CAMBODIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will promote a stable or increasing population of White-shouldered Ibis in Western Siem Pang Forest and Lomphat Wildlife Sanctuary. The grantee will undertake an innovative method to create additional habitat; specific objectives include: (1) Playback of bird calls; (2) The use of dolly (model) birds to encourage live birds to join new communal roosting sites; (3) The enhancement of preferred White-shouldered Ibis foraging habitat by the digging of forest pools trapeangs as key foraging resources for the species.</narrative>
  </description>
